    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.is_edge_cover - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.is_edge_cover.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_edge_cover()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a set of edges touches every node (an edge cover).\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_edge_cover()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a set of edges touches every node (an edge cover).\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.is_edge_cover()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Check if a set of edges touches every node (an edge cover).\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCheck if a set of edges touches every node (an edge cover).\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L77355-L77433){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.is_edge_cover(edges)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Is edge cover](../assets/graphs/is-edge-cover.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The path A-B-C-D on both sides, with the candidate edges drawn as the input. Left: the outer edges A-B and C-D touch all four nodes, so is_edge_cover() returns True. Right: the middle edge B-C alone misses A and D (filled in the accent color), so is_edge_cover() returns False.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nAn edge cover is a set of edges such that every node of the graph is an endpoint of at\nleast one of them. Unlike a matching, edges in a cover may share endpoints. Use this\nmethod to validate a hand-built cover or the output of `minimum_edge_cover()`. A graph with\nan isolated node has no edge cover, so the check is then always `False` (and the empty\ngraph is covered by the empty set).\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[edges]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [list[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A list of integer edge IDs.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `True` if every node is an endpoint of one of the edges. Unknown edge IDs give\n    `False`.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThe check collects the endpoints of the given edges and compares them with the node\nset, in $O(V + k)$ time for $k$ edges. Edge direction is ignored.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~minimum_edge_cover`) \n\n:   Find the fewest edges that touch every node.\n\n[](`~is_vertex_cover`) \n\n:   Check that a set of nodes touches every edge.\n\n[](`~is_matching`) \n\n:   Check that no two edges share a node.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe two outer edges of the path `A`-`B`-`C`-`D` touch all four nodes, while the middle\nedge alone misses `A` and `D`:\n\n::: {#500e375c .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npath = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\nab, bc, cd = (\n    path.find_edge_ids(u, v)[0]\n    for u, v in [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")]\n)\n\npath.is_edge_cover([ab, cd]), path.is_edge_cover([bc])\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(True, False)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Someone for every task, a task for everyone\n\n`teams()` links the 8 workers of a made-up software team, and the contractor Quinn, to\nthe 8 tasks of a release that each can do. The cheapest assignment covers every task\nbut leaves Luis without one, so it isn't an edge cover. Pairing Luis with Mei on Design\nmakes it one:\n\n::: {#e2d71382 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nteam = ec.teams(contractor=True)\nplan = team.bipartite_minimum_weight_full_matching()\npaired = plan + team.find_edge_ids(\"Luis\", \"Design\")\n\nteam.is_edge_cover(plan), team.is_edge_cover(paired)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(False, True)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#2cf8530a .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nteam.layout_bipartite(align=\"horizontal\", aspect_ratio=0.4).plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", highlight_edges=paired, label_by=\"label\", height=300\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode